[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b20: cluster morphology
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   The comet channel (step_18) found the anomaly is a
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   THRESHOLD, not a peak: flat excess inside a ~60-75 deg
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   patch, then a step down to background -- "the shape of a
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   wall, not a mass."  The same question on the TNO side:
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   is the detached varpi cluster peaked (von Mises -- a
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   directional pull toward the axis) or flat-topped (a
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   cap-uniform plateau -- a boundary sector)?
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   The raw profile says top-hat: ~flat inside 60 deg, then a
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   depleted ring at 60-90 deg, then far-field uniform.  This
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   step formalizes it.
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   M1  Angular profile of detached varpi about the axis.
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   M2  Model comparison on the unbinned offsets:
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   (a) uniform + von Mises cluster   (b13's model)
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   (b) uniform + top-hat sector of half-width W
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   (c) uniform only
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   -- AIC on maximum likelihood.
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   M3  The deficit ring: fraction of objects at 60-90 deg
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   vs the uniform expectation -- a real boundary has an
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   outside as well as an inside.
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   M4  In-cap flatness: chi2 uniformity of the 26 in-cap
[2026-09-20 10:47:30 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 055]   objects' internal distribution.
